+## FAQ
+
+### What are the best open source AI tools for accountants in 2026?
+For most teams, the strongest starting stack is [PaddleOCR](https://github.com/PaddlePaddle/PaddleOCR) or [OCRmyPDF](https://github.com/ocrmypdf/OCRmyPDF) for document intake, [paperless-ngx](https://github.com/paperless-ngx/paperless-ngx) for searchable archives, [PandasAI](https://github.com/sinaptik-ai/pandas-ai) or [Vanna](https://github.com/vanna-ai/vanna) for data questions, and [Great Expectations](https://github.com/great-expectations/great_expectations) for controls. If forecasting matters, add [Prophet](https://github.com/facebook/prophet) or [Darts](https://github.com/unit8co/darts).
+
+### Are there truly self-hosted AI tools for accountants on GitHub?
+Yes. Every tool in this repository is a public GitHub repository, and most can be self-hosted or embedded into an internal workflow. That said, some projects optionally integrate with external LLM APIs, so self-hosting feasibility still depends on your model and infrastructure choices.
+
+### Which open source GitHub repos help accountants process invoices and receipts?
+The strongest options in this list are [PaddleOCR](https://github.com/PaddlePaddle/PaddleOCR), [OCRmyPDF](https://github.com/ocrmypdf/OCRmyPDF), [Documind](https://github.com/DocumindHQ/documind), [paperless-ngx](https://github.com/paperless-ngx/paperless-ngx), and [tesseract.js](https://github.com/naptha/tesseract.js). They cover OCR, structured extraction, PDF conversion, and searchable archives.
+
+### Which GitHub projects let accountants ask questions of SQL databases in natural language?
+[Vanna](https://github.com/vanna-ai/vanna), [WrenAI](https://github.com/Canner/WrenAI), [SQL Chat](https://github.com/sqlchat/sqlchat), [Dataherald](https://github.com/Dataherald/dataherald), and [PandasAI](https://github.com/sinaptik-ai/pandas-ai) all address this need in different ways. Choose based on whether you want a lightweight assistant, a chat-first SQL client, or a broader self-hosted BI layer.
+
+### What open source AI tools help with budgeting, revenue forecasting, and anomaly detection?
+[Prophet](https://github.com/facebook/prophet), [sktime](https://github.com/sktime/sktime), [Darts](https://github.com/unit8co/darts), [AutoGluon](https://github.com/autogluon/autogluon), and [PyCaret](https://github.com/pycaret/pycaret) are the best starting points in this repo for finance forecasting and abnormal-pattern detection.
+
+### Are there enough mature accounting-specific AI repositories on GitHub?
+Not really. That is the main gap this research exposed. Pure “AI for accountants” repos on GitHub are sparse and often immature, so this list honestly broadens into adjacent open-source tools that accountants actually use in production workflows: OCR, document intelligence, SQL copilots, forecasting, and controls.
+
+### How should an accounting team evaluate one of these repositories before adoption?
+Check the license first, then maintenance recency, issue activity, deployment model, and whether the repo can work with your existing finance stack. For regulated teams, also review data residency, auditability, and whether the tool can run fully inside your environment.
+
